              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कदलीफलम् (kadalīphalam) — \"a banana\": कदली, \"the banana plant\", with फलम्, \"fruit\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kadalīphala is a compound of kadalī, \"the banana plant\", and phala, \"fruit\". CDIAL 2712 takes kadalī as borrowed from an Austroasiatic language; it lives on as Hindi kelā, \"banana\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plant plus fruit."
